Stop applying the 15 minute cooldown for completing a random dungeon.
Touches: src/server/game/DungeonFinding/LFGMgr.cpp, LFGMgr::TeleportPlayer path

Why: player request. LFG_SPELL_DUNGEON_COOLDOWN (71328) exists to pace a
retail-sized population off the random-dungeon reward. On a realm with a
handful of concurrent players it only stops those players from immediately
running something else together, which is the opposite of what the finder
is for here.

Only the completion cooldown goes. The 150 second penalty applied further
down for DECLINING or timing out on a proposal is deliberately kept -- that
one is not about pacing rewards, it exists so one player cannot repeatedly
collapse other people's groups at no cost.

The `randomDungeon` flag is still set, because the teleport bookkeeping
below it reads the flag. The join-time HasAura(LFG_SPELL_DUNGEON_COOLDOWN)
checks are left alone; with the completion cooldown never applied they now
only ever gate someone serving the decline penalty, which is correct.

--- a/src/server/game/DungeonFinding/LFGMgr.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/DungeonFinding/LFGMgr.cpp
@@ teleport loop, "Add the cooldown spell if queued for a random dungeon"
-                if ((randomDungeon || selectedRandomLfgDungeon(player->GetGUID())) && !player->HasAura(LFG_SPELL_DUNGEON_COOLDOWN))
+                if (randomDungeon || selectedRandomLfgDungeon(player->GetGUID()))
                 {
                     randomDungeon = true;
-                    // if player is debugging, don't add dungeon cooldown
-                    if (!m_Testing)
-                    {
-                        player->AddAura(LFG_SPELL_DUNGEON_COOLDOWN, player);
-                    }
                 }
